WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:09.333 --> 00:00:12.375
Kimberly: Well, this
place is an insane mess!

00:00:12.375 --> 00:00:14.958
Allison: This is
all my game fuel.

00:00:14.958 --> 00:00:17.125
I have no time for trash.

00:00:17.125 --> 00:00:19.042
Kimberly: It’s not trash!

00:00:19.042 --> 00:00:21.542
This is all recyclable!

00:00:21.542 --> 00:00:24.708
Anyway, aren’t you supposed
to be working on homework?

00:00:24.708 --> 00:00:26.000
Allison: Homework!

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:29.500
I don’t have time for that
monotonous, repetitive work.

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:34.000
I am almost level 40 on
World of Plasticracft!

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:37.417
I just have to collect 3 more
water bottles with the number 2

00:00:37.417 --> 00:00:40.583
imprinted on them, take them to
the high elvish recyclomancer

00:00:40.583 --> 00:00:44.208
and then I’ll be able to cast
malleability 3 times per day

00:00:44.208 --> 00:00:47.083
on any random
encounters below level 5.

00:00:47.083 --> 00:00:49.375
These are important things!

00:00:49.375 --> 00:00:52.792
Kimberly: I stopped listening
after you said “World”.

00:00:52.792 --> 00:00:54.917
Allison: this game has
educational garbage

00:00:54.917 --> 00:00:58.500
I never pay attention to, you
can probably help with that.

00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:00.333
Log on to Mom’s computer.

00:01:00.333 --> 00:01:03.000
Kimberly: I cannot believe
you’ve talked me into

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:05.250
this nerd stuff…

00:01:06.250 --> 00:01:11.542
Password... Y-E-S. Enter.

00:01:11.542 --> 00:01:12.667
Oh, Gosh.

00:01:14.708 --> 00:01:16.875
Well, this is magical!

00:01:17.583 --> 00:01:18.958
WAH!

00:01:20.458 --> 00:01:24.042
Allison: Welcome to Plasteroth!

00:01:24.042 --> 00:01:26.667
Kimberly: This place is a dump!

00:01:26.667 --> 00:01:29.292
Don’t you guys ever recycle?

00:01:29.292 --> 00:01:31.000
Allison: Recycle?!

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:32.875
Are you kidding?!

00:01:32.875 --> 00:01:35.667
When you’re adventuring and
your bag of holding gets full,

00:01:35.667 --> 00:01:38.083
you just gotta drop that item.

00:01:38.083 --> 00:01:39.792
Kimberly: But these
are all plastic!

00:01:39.792 --> 00:01:43.583
Many of these can
easily be recycled!

00:01:43.583 --> 00:01:46.375
Blort: Back for more,
little orc?!

00:01:46.375 --> 00:01:48.333
Allison: Not again!

00:01:48.333 --> 00:01:49.917
Kimberly: Who is this?

00:01:49.917 --> 00:01:52.292
Allison: He’s Blort
the Corpulent.

00:01:52.292 --> 00:01:55.625
I can’t prove it yet,
but I think he’s 32 and

00:01:55.625 --> 00:01:57.667
lives in his mom’s basement.

00:01:57.667 --> 00:01:58.625
Blort: Wrong!

00:01:58.625 --> 00:02:02.042
28 and my aunt’s attic!

00:02:02.042 --> 00:02:03.375
Have at thee!

00:02:06.042 --> 00:02:07.792
Kimberly: Ah, gross!

00:02:07.792 --> 00:02:09.708
Where are we?

00:02:09.708 --> 00:02:10.958
Allison: Blort got us.

00:02:10.958 --> 00:02:13.625
we re-spawned in the graveyard.

00:02:13.625 --> 00:02:15.458
Pollymer: Haldo, travelers!

00:02:15.458 --> 00:02:18.167
It would appear
to mine eyes that

00:02:18.167 --> 00:02:20.625
thou art experiencing
difficulties.

00:02:20.625 --> 00:02:22.167
Allison: Who are you?

00:02:22.167 --> 00:02:24.792
Pollymer: Greetings and
salutations,

00:02:24.792 --> 00:02:30.958
I am Lady Polly of Mer and I...
Ok, I can’t do that anymore.

00:02:30.958 --> 00:02:32.625
I’m Pollymer.

00:02:32.625 --> 00:02:36.417
If you want to beat Blort, you
need to learn how to recycle.

00:02:36.417 --> 00:02:37.708
Follow me.

00:02:37.708 --> 00:02:39.250
Kimberly: Told you so!

00:02:39.250 --> 00:02:41.292
Allison: This game had better
not be tricking me into

00:02:41.292 --> 00:02:42.917
being a better person!

00:02:42.917 --> 00:02:45.875
Pollymer: In Plasteroth, all of
our items and loot are made of

00:02:45.875 --> 00:02:49.542
plastics, but the best players
don’t throw out old loot,

00:02:49.542 --> 00:02:52.000
they recycle their
unwanted items.

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:53.250
Allison: Ok, fine.

00:02:53.250 --> 00:02:57.167
Let’s gather this junk up and
throw it in the recycling bin.

00:02:57.167 --> 00:02:58.542
Kimberly: You can’t do that!

00:02:58.542 --> 00:03:00.583
All these plastics
are different!

00:03:00.583 --> 00:03:02.417
Allison: Plastic is plastic.

00:03:02.417 --> 00:03:03.958
Pollymer: Your sister is right.

00:03:03.958 --> 00:03:05.208
Kimberly: Again.

00:03:05.208 --> 00:03:07.625
Pollymer: Haven’t you ever
noticed those numbers on

00:03:07.625 --> 00:03:09.542
the bottom of items?

00:03:09.542 --> 00:03:11.708
Allison: I always assumed
those were stats that only

00:03:11.708 --> 00:03:14.042
uber nerds paid attention to.

00:03:14.042 --> 00:03:17.417
Pollymer: you are not wrong,
but those numbers also tell you

00:03:17.417 --> 00:03:20.333
the kind of plastic
that item is made of.

00:03:20.333 --> 00:03:23.500
There are 7 basic
types of plastic.

00:03:23.500 --> 00:03:27.333
You can usually find the number
in a triangle shaped recycling

00:03:27.333 --> 00:03:29.625
symbol on the bottom
of the product.

00:03:29.625 --> 00:03:33.083
These numbers are the resin
identification code.

00:03:33.083 --> 00:03:36.500
The code is used internationally
and tells us whether we can

00:03:36.500 --> 00:03:38.250
recycle the plastic or not.

00:03:38.250 --> 00:03:42.500
Plastics are made of sheets of
long chemicals Called polymers.

00:03:42.500 --> 00:03:45.708
Different plastics are
made of different polymers.

00:03:45.708 --> 00:03:49.000
Between those sheets are
plasticizer chemicals that

00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:51.083
give plastics their properties.

00:03:51.083 --> 00:03:54.333
These chemicals can make
plastics harder, softer,

00:03:54.333 --> 00:03:56.542
smooth, or flexible.

00:03:56.542 --> 00:03:58.750
There’s a lot going on in there.

00:03:58.750 --> 00:04:02.500
Plastics 1 and 2 are the
most commonly recycled

00:04:02.500 --> 00:04:03.917
types of plastic.

00:04:03.917 --> 00:04:07.917
Most types of bottles are
made using plastics 1 and 2.

00:04:07.917 --> 00:04:11.625
Allison: So types 1 and 2
can be recycled anywhere?

00:04:11.625 --> 00:04:14.833
Pollymer: Probably,
but you have to check.

00:04:14.833 --> 00:04:19.000
Plastics 4, 5, and 6 are
the next most recycled.

00:04:19.000 --> 00:04:21.958
These plastics are very
common in food wraps,

00:04:21.958 --> 00:04:25.667
Straws and styrofoam that
people usually throw out.

00:04:25.667 --> 00:04:28.000
These plastics can be
tricky to recycle, and

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:29.917
not all areas accept them.

00:04:29.917 --> 00:04:31.792
Allison: didn’t you skip one?

00:04:31.792 --> 00:04:33.625
Pollymer: Yeah, number 3.

00:04:33.625 --> 00:04:36.083
These plastics are
made with vinyl, and

00:04:36.083 --> 00:04:37.833
they are rarely recycled.

00:04:37.833 --> 00:04:41.292
There’s just not much demand
for plastic 3 as a recyclable.

00:04:41.292 --> 00:04:44.125
Kimberly: weren’t there
7 types of plastic?

00:04:44.125 --> 00:04:45.292
Pollymer: Correct!

00:04:45.292 --> 00:04:48.000
If the plastic doesn’t fit
into the other groups, or

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:51.583
it’s made of a mixture
of plastics, it’s a 7.

00:04:51.583 --> 00:04:54.208
This plastic has become
controversial because

00:04:54.208 --> 00:04:56.958
they often include a
chemical known as BPA,

00:04:56.958 --> 00:05:00.167
which comes with health
Concerns if ingested.

00:05:00.167 --> 00:05:03.125
Because this plastic is so
inconsistent, not many

00:05:03.125 --> 00:05:05.750
recycling programs
take plastic 7...

00:05:05.750 --> 00:05:10.250
In Plasteroth, few master
the magics of recycling.

00:05:10.250 --> 00:05:13.958
Legend tells of a warrior
that can wield a blade

00:05:13.958 --> 00:05:16.542
made of all the
elemental plastics,

00:05:16.542 --> 00:05:21.083
Recy’klar, destroyer of wastes.

00:05:21.083 --> 00:05:22.792
Allison: Epic loot?!

00:05:22.792 --> 00:05:24.167
Let’s sort this plastic!

00:05:24.167 --> 00:05:28.000
Kimberly: Well, that depends
what plastics can be taken in

00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:30.333
Plasteroth’s recycling program.

00:05:30.333 --> 00:05:33.083
Allison: You mean they
don’t just take it all?

00:05:33.083 --> 00:05:34.833
Pollymer: not in all areas.

00:05:34.833 --> 00:05:37.958
Every area of the country takes
different plastic numbers

00:05:37.958 --> 00:05:39.333
in their recycling.

00:05:39.333 --> 00:05:44.875
So while plastics 1,2,3,4,5 and
7 may be recyclable In

00:05:44.875 --> 00:05:48.542
Sheboygan, Wisconsin,
they may not take Plastic 7

00:05:48.542 --> 00:05:50.542
in Pittsburg, Pennsylvania.

00:05:50.542 --> 00:05:53.000
Joey-the-recycling guy: Hey,
What I tell yinz kids about

00:05:53.000 --> 00:05:55.292
puttin’ plastic 7
in a recyclin’?

00:05:55.292 --> 00:05:58.375
Aww, they’ll throw
that whole bin awt.

00:05:58.375 --> 00:06:01.875
Pollymer: Even if your area
doesn’t take some plastics,

00:06:01.875 --> 00:06:05.333
many grocery stores will
recycle your plastic bags, and

00:06:05.333 --> 00:06:09.417
electronic stores often
recycle disks and old devices.

00:06:09.417 --> 00:06:13.500
With some effort, very little
should be going to the landfill.

00:06:13.500 --> 00:06:18.292
Fortunately, here in Plasteroth,
we take all seven plastics.

00:06:18.292 --> 00:06:20.292
Allison: all in the same bin?

00:06:20.292 --> 00:06:21.500
Pollymer: Uh huh

00:06:21.500 --> 00:06:22.917
Allison: DIDN’T
I SAY THAT LIKE THREE

00:06:22.917 --> 00:06:25.000
EXPOSITION HEAVY
LECTURES AGO?!

00:06:25.000 --> 00:06:27.833
Kimberly: Yeah,
but now you know why!

00:06:27.833 --> 00:06:30.250
Pollymer: Come on,
Let’s take this plastic

00:06:30.250 --> 00:06:31.792
to the recycling forge.

00:06:31.792 --> 00:06:34.583
Allison: I can’t believe
Kimberly managed to

00:06:34.583 --> 00:06:36.375
ruin video games!

00:06:36.375 --> 00:06:38.250
This is him?!

00:06:38.250 --> 00:06:40.708
I thought elves were,
like… attractive…

00:06:40.708 --> 00:06:42.042
with bows and arrows…

00:06:42.042 --> 00:06:44.958
Kimberly: and less burgers.

00:06:44.958 --> 00:06:48.375
Pollymer: Just like
America, fewer than 30% of

00:06:48.375 --> 00:06:51.708
Plasteroth players
use recycling forges.

00:06:51.708 --> 00:06:53.417
There is demand
for the material,

00:06:53.417 --> 00:06:55.708
but not enough
people bother.

00:06:55.708 --> 00:06:57.875
HALDO SMITHY!

00:06:57.875 --> 00:06:59.875
Smithy: Goodness!
Who goes there?

00:06:59.875 --> 00:07:04.000
Kimberly: Three adventurers
seeking your services… Sir.

00:07:04.000 --> 00:07:05.875
Smithy: I used to
be an adventurer.

00:07:05.875 --> 00:07:09.958
Then I took a high density
polyethylene arrow to the knee.

00:07:09.958 --> 00:07:13.125
Pollymer: We have brought
the 7 elemental plastics.

00:07:13.125 --> 00:07:20.625
We seek to forge Recy’klar,
Destroyer of Wastes!

00:07:20.625 --> 00:07:24.250
Smithy: So, you seek the
blade of heroes, eh?

00:07:24.250 --> 00:07:25.208
Best get to it then.

00:07:25.208 --> 00:07:28.833
The first thing you have to know
about plastic recycling is that

00:07:28.833 --> 00:07:31.583
you rarely make the
same thing twice.

00:07:31.583 --> 00:07:35.583
If you bring me a soda bottle, I
can’t recycle the materials into

00:07:35.583 --> 00:07:38.667
a new soda bottle, the
material’s different.

00:07:38.667 --> 00:07:42.125
When I get plastics, I
have to sort them by type.

00:07:42.125 --> 00:07:47.167
I can’t mix type 1 plastics
with type 5 plastics.

00:07:47.167 --> 00:07:49.667
Then we grind the
plastic into chips.

00:07:49.667 --> 00:07:52.833
All of the labels and bits of
glue are in the way at this

00:07:52.833 --> 00:07:56.958
point, so we will need to
wash and bathe the chips.

00:07:56.958 --> 00:08:00.583
After they dry, we melt
the chips into pellets.

00:08:00.583 --> 00:08:04.125
These pellets can be
used to make new items.

00:08:04.125 --> 00:08:07.875
Most recycled plastics can
become polar fleece,

00:08:07.875 --> 00:08:11.583
tote bags, containers,
furniture, insulation,

00:08:11.583 --> 00:08:13.792
brushes, lots of things!

00:08:13.792 --> 00:08:16.917
But today in my
forge, we’ve made…

00:08:16.917 --> 00:08:23.417
Recy’klar! Destroyer of Wastes!

00:08:23.417 --> 00:08:28.000
Mike: Please, Blort, don’t send
me back to the graveyard!

00:08:28.000 --> 00:08:31.958
Blort: This validates
me as a person!

00:08:31.958 --> 00:08:35.417
Hahaha!!

00:08:35.417 --> 00:08:37.417
All too easy…

00:08:37.417 --> 00:08:39.625
Allison: Stand down, Blort!

00:08:39.625 --> 00:08:42.208
Blort: Back again, young maiden?

00:08:42.208 --> 00:08:47.833
Allison: Behold Recy’klar!
Destroyer of Wastes!

00:08:47.833 --> 00:08:50.625
Your days of looting
and polluting are done!

00:08:50.625 --> 00:08:51.792
Hah!

00:08:51.792 --> 00:08:54.000
A recycled blade?

00:08:54.000 --> 00:08:57.792
The only way to win in this
world is to buy the newest,

00:08:57.792 --> 00:08:59.917
nicest loot.

00:08:59.917 --> 00:09:02.250
Pollymer: That’s not going
to work forever, Blort!

00:09:02.250 --> 00:09:05.083
We only have so many
raw materials to make

00:09:05.083 --> 00:09:07.083
new plastics on this planet!

00:09:07.083 --> 00:09:09.167
And where do we
put all the waste?

00:09:09.167 --> 00:09:12.208
This stuff just sits
in a landfill forever.

00:09:12.208 --> 00:09:16.708
We don’t know how long plastics
last, and some of them release

00:09:16.708 --> 00:09:20.167
harmful chemicals into our
bodies and the environment.

00:09:20.167 --> 00:09:22.792
Blort: Enough talk!

00:09:22.792 --> 00:09:24.375
Allison: I agree!

00:09:24.375 --> 00:09:27.833
Blort: Whatever, my aunt’s
calling me for dinner anyway.

00:09:30.750 --> 00:09:34.417
Kimberly: Well, I have to say,
Allison, I actually learned

00:09:34.417 --> 00:09:36.083
a lot from that game.

00:09:36.083 --> 00:09:38.917
Our world doesn’t have
infinite resources.

00:09:38.917 --> 00:09:41.375
We need to care about recycling.

00:09:41.375 --> 00:09:44.917
It’s important to check the
numbers on our plastics so

00:09:44.917 --> 00:09:48.917
you can make sure that you’re
recycling the right materials.

00:09:48.917 --> 00:09:52.542
So, Allison, are you going
to recycle all this junk?

00:09:52.542 --> 00:09:53.125
Allison: What?

00:09:53.125 --> 00:09:56.583
You expect me to apply a lesson
from a game to real life?

00:09:56.583 --> 00:09:58.208
Kimberly: Recycle it!!!

00:10:09.240 --> 00:10:11.620
Auntie: Blart, come to dinner!

00:10:11.620 --> 00:10:14.899
Blart: But people are wrong on the Internet!!

00:10:14.899 --> 00:10:16.429
Auntie: Now!

00:10:16.429 --> 00:10:17.620
Blart: Yes, Auntie.

